                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I purchased this game not knowing what to expect. After about an hour and completing the first level, I found this to bring a lot of investigative elements to this psychological thriller. \n\nYou play James Sachs, and you are investigating 2 murders when things start messing with your head. You go through the game finding clues, putting 2 and 2 together, and solving some complex puzzles. It is a short game, around 5 hours, but there is a lot to the story and you will not get bored.\n\n+Pros\nGood Graphics\nInteresting detective/investigating point and click element\nA story where you want to know what happens next, and can't stop playing even after you do.\n\n-I threw a beer bottle at the window because I was searching for the next step, it did not shatter. Made me want a beer.\n\n+Cons\nReally only one at the moment, the movement seems a bit laggy in response time, especially the sprint.\n\nDefiniterly worth the 10 dollars (now 8.99 until Feb 2nd).\n\n9/10 - Would throw beer bottles at the window again to enhance my creative juices\n\nI made a part 1 video, you can check out the gameplay. Nicely done dev.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zVS8o3UdhNk",
